From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:38:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: drop redundant GTest system include

The openEuler GTest CMake targets export /usr/include.  In the RVA23 QEMU
buildroot CMake does not discover the compiler's implicit C++ include list,
so it emits -isystem /usr/include.  That makes libstdc++'s include_next lookup
for stdlib.h skip the only system copy.  Remove only this compiler-default
path while retaining any non-default include paths exported by GTest.

Root cause: the imported GTest targets expose a compiler-default include as a
system include while CMake's QEMU buildroot probe omits that same default from
its implicit include set.
Patch-Source: downstream reconstruction from the observed openEuler RVA23 build
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (the trigger is downstream toolchain metadata)
Removal: remove when the locked openEuler CMake/GTest buildroot no longer emits
         /usr/include as a redundant imported-target system include.

---
 test/CMakeLists.txt | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/CMakeLists.txt b/test/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -14,6 +14,21 @@
 IF (CMAKE_VERSION VERSION_LESS "3.23.0")
   Message("GoogleTest found, cmake version too old to verify GMock, look for errors...")
 ELSE ()
+  foreach(gtest_target GTest::gtest GTest::gmock)
+    if(TARGET ${gtest_target})
+      foreach(include_property
+              INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES
+              INTERFACE_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES)
+        get_target_property(gtest_includes ${gtest_target} ${include_property})
+        if(gtest_includes)
+          list(REMOVE_ITEM gtest_includes "/usr/include")
+          set_target_properties(${gtest_target} PROPERTIES
+            ${include_property} "${gtest_includes}")
+        endif()
+      endforeach()
+    endif()
+  endforeach()
+
   IF (NOT TARGET GTest::gmock)
     Message(FATAL_ERROR "GoogleTest found but the GMock component was not found")
   ENDIF()
